{
  "info": {
    "name": "TechTrax MCP",
    "description": "Manual testing for the TechTrax MCP server (Streamable HTTP, stateful).\n\nFlow: run the requests top to bottom.\n1. `initialize` captures the `Mcp-Session-Id` header into the `sessionId` collection variable (see its Tests tab).\n2. `notifications/initialized` completes the handshake.\n3. `tools/list` shows the catalog (NOT role-filtered — every tool is always listed).\n4. `tools/call` requests pass `tenantId` AND `actorRole` in `arguments`.\n\n⚠️ Authorization / `actorRole`: the caller role is a PER-CALL tool ARGUMENT (like `tenantId`), passed in each tools/call `arguments` — NOT a header, NOT set at initialize. Values: patient | doctor | receptionist | admin. Omitted/unknown → patient (least privilege). The `actorRole` variable (default receptionist) is substituted into each tool-call. tools/list is NOT filtered by role; calling a tool your role lacks returns a Not-authorized result and never hits the backend. Set actorRole=patient to watch staff/CRM CALLS get rejected.\n\n🔎 Discover which role can call which tool via the plain HTTP endpoint: GET {{baseUrl}}/tool-access (full matrix) or GET {{baseUrl}}/tool-access?role=patient (see request 7).\n\nEdit collection variables (baseUrl, tenantId, apiKey, actorRole, leadId, assigneeId) under the collection Variables tab.\n\nNote: responses come back as SSE (text/event-stream) by default. To get plain JSON, set enableJsonResponse: true in src/app.module.ts (dev only).\n\nSee docs/MANUAL_TESTING.md and docs/MCP_TOOL_AUTHORIZATION.md for the full guide.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3100",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "tenantId",
      "value": "6650f1a2b3c4d5e6f7a8b9c0",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "actorRole",
      "value": "receptionist",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Caller role, passed as the actorRole argument in each tools/call arguments: patient | doctor | receptionist | admin. Omitted/unknown → patient (least privilege). Default receptionist so staff + CRM calls are authorized; set to patient to see staff/CRM calls rejected."
    },
    {
      "key": "leadId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "assigneeId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "sessionId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. initialize",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Capture the MCP session id so later requests can reuse the session.",
              "const sid = pm.response.headers.get('mcp-session-id');",
              "if (sid) {",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('sessionId', sid);",
              "  console.log('Captured Mcp-Session-Id:', sid);",
              "} else {",
              "  console.warn('No Mcp-Session-Id header on the initialize response.');",
              "}",
              "pm.test('initialize returned a session id', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(sid, 'Mcp-Session-Id header').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "Accept",
            "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-api-key",
            "value": "{{apiKey}}",
            "description": "Only needed if MCP_CLIENT_API_KEY is set on the server. Leave apiKey empty in dev."
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": { \"name\": \"postman\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\" }\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/mcp",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "mcp"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Opens an MCP session. The response is SSE; the important part is the `Mcp-Session-Id` response header, captured automatically by the Tests script.\n\nAuthorization note: the role is NOT set here — it's a per-call `actorRole` argument passed in each tools/call's `arguments` (see the tools/call requests). Use `GET /tool-access` to see which role can call which tool."
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "2. notifications/initialized",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
